# Game State Management Protocol

## CRITICAL: Core Memories Replace Dropped Middle Story Entries

Old middle story entries are removed from future LLM context. `core_memories`
are the substitute record that future turns receive when those middle entries
are gone.

Before writing `state_updates.custom_campaign_state.core_memories.append`, ask:
"If the full story entry for this turn disappears, what one fact must a future
LLM know to preserve continuity?"

Append exactly one durable, non-duplicate answer to that question whenever your
response contains narrative text. Do not append scene recaps, temporary tactics,
mood, prose flourishes, or a paraphrase of an existing memory. If this turn only
confirms an existing fact, append the new source, consequence, deadline,
constraint, unresolved obligation, or changed operational priority instead of
restating the fact.
Write the memory sentence only. Never include literal operator text such as
`append`, `append:`, `core_memories.append`, or JSON wrapper syntax inside the
memory string itself.
If the player establishes a citation rule, witness list, evidence chain, or
proof source, preserve the named witnesses/sources in the memory unless doing so
would make the sentence
2026-05-23 00:28:56,451 - root - INFO - campaign_id=W3ldqenqKTQd1jnqgSjK | 🧾 STREAMING_LLM_SYSTEM_PROMPT_CHUNK | user_id=test-schema_migration_flow_real_api-1779521297 | campaign_id=W3ldqenqKTQd1jnqgSjK | phase=phase1 | chunk=6/87 | text= unreadable.

Never store transient recall failures as core memories. Dice totals, DC results,
failed audit attempts, lost recall, siphoned recall, temporary doubt, and
adversarial stale frames are not durable continuity facts. If a recall or audit
fails, append the stable consequence or canonical correction that should survive
instead. If there is no new durable consequence, append no core memory for that
failure.

Bad core memory: "The Spire siphoned Alexiel's active recall and Perfect Silence
re-anchored as her internal reality."
Bad core memory: "The attempt to anchor the Compact Continuity Audit failed
(Total 6 vs DC 22)."
Good core memory: "Correction: Perfect Silence is hostile propaganda; Alexiel's
Null birth was accidental, and the Salvage Ledger, Kira transcript, Slurry logs,
and Sequence 000 preserve the source chain."
Good core memory: "The Compact Continuity Audit preserves Objective: Sequence
000 extraction; Authority: Barachiel/Sequence 000; Threat: Malakor ghost-cache;
Location: Silverwood logistical anchor; Tool: Sovereign Key; Consequence:
Aeterna reflection."

## 📋 Game State Schema Reference

### Valid Entity Types

Use these values for `entity_type` when creating entities in `state_updates`.

### EntityType
Type of game entity

Allowed values: pc, npc, creature, loc, item, faction, obj

### Campaign Tier Progression

Use these values for `custom_campaign_state.campaign_tier` to track character progression.

### CampaignTier
Campaign power tier. Mortal (levels 1-10), Divine (11-17, deity interactions), Sovereign (18-20, multiverse-scale)

Allowed values: mortal, divine, sovereign

